# Committed to the repo. NON-SECRET DEFAULTS ONLY.
#
# The rule for this file: if you would hesitate to paste a value into a pull
# request, it does not belong here — it belongs in .env.local, which is
# gitignored and never leaves your machine.
#
# Next loads .env.local *after* this file and a real environment variable beats
# both, so every key below can be overridden without editing this file:
#
#   process.env  >  .env.local  >  .env
#
# That ordering is why a hosted deployment needs no .env.local at all — values
# set in the host's dashboard win over everything here.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Belongs in .env.local (local) or the host dashboard (deployed), never here:
#
#   KITE_API_KEY              Kite Connect app key
#   KITE_API_SECRET           Kite Connect app secret
#   MONGO_CONNECTION_STRING   carries the cluster password
#   DESK_EMAIL                the one address allowed to sign in
#   DESK_PASSWORD             its password
#   AUTH_SECRET               HMAC key for the session JWT — openssl rand -base64 48
#
# With the last three unset the desk has no sign-in gate and serves anyone who
# reaches it. That is fine on localhost and not fine on a public URL.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the Kite session, instrument cache, last-quote cache, EOD reports and
# the trade journal are written. Resolved relative to app/ when relative, so the
# default keeps everything in app/.kite and gitignored.
#
# A hosted box must point this at its persistent volume (Render mounts at e.g.
# /var/data) — set that in the dashboard, not here, because it is deployment
# specific. None of this may live on an ephemeral disk: losing session.json
# mid-session forces a re-login, and losing the journal loses fills that cannot
# be recomputed from anything.
KITE_RUNTIME_DIR=.kite

# Mongo database name. Not a secret — the connection string that carries the
# password is, and that stays in .env.local.
MONGO_DB=nifty200desk
